{
  "id": "https://fredbrug.github.io/skohub-pages/pfdp/data-curation",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "Data curation",
    "nl": "Datacuratie"
  },
  "altLabel": {
    "en": [
      "Curation of data"
    ],
    "nl": [
      "Curatie van data"
    ]
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "The active selection, appraisal, organization, description, quality control, preservation, and enhancement of data to support continued access and reuse.",
    "nl": "De actieve selectie, waardering, organisatie, beschrijving, kwaliteitscontrole, preservering en verrijking van data ter ondersteuning van blijvende toegang en hergebruik."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "A managed process, throughout the data lifecycle, by which data/data collections are cleansed, documented, standardized, formatted and inter-related. This includes versioning data, or forming a new collection from several data sources, annotating with metadata, adding codes to raw data (e.g., classifying a galaxy \nimage with a galaxy type such as “spiral”). Higher levels of curation involve maintaining links with annotation and with other published materials. Thus, a dataset may include a \ncitation link to publication whose analysis was based on the data. The goal of curation is to manage and promote the use of data from its point of creation to ensure it is fit for contemporary purpose and available for discovery and re-use. For dynamic datasets this may mean continuous enrichment or updating to keep it fit for purpose. Special forms of curation may be available in data repositories. The data curation process itself must be documented as part of curation. Thus, curation and provenance are highly related. https://codata.org/rdm\nterminology/data-curation/)"
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "DC"
  ],
